{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And tomorrow I shall do.</b> That is, she says, 'my request.' In my view Esther delayed speaking on the first day at the wine banquet because she saw no sign that HaShem had renewed [action] on account of Israel's fast, as He did on the second day through the matter of the greatness of Mordecai — [then] her heart was strengthened."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The verb חידש is understood as 'renewed' i.e. brought about anew; the subject is HaShem. On the second day, Ibn Ezra alludes to the events of Esther 6 (the king's sleepless night)."}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:02.461609989Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}